<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Accessibility Audit Report — Aranjmaa Lkhamaa</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --accent: #1E7466;
    --accent-dark: #175E53;
    --accent-tint: #E8F2EF;
    --text: #172B2A;
    --muted: #5F6E6A;
    --border: #E2E9E6;
    --bad: #9C3B22;
    --bad-tint: #FBEDE8;
  }

  * { box-sizing: border-box; }

  body {
    font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
    padding: 40px 20px;
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    color: var(--text);
    line-height: 1.7;
    background: #F3F6F5;
  }

  .container {
    background: #FFFFFF;
    padding: 44px;
    border-radius: 16px;
    border-top: 5px solid var(--accent);
    box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(23, 43, 42, 0.06);
  }

  h1 { font-size: 30px; font-weight: 800; margin: 0 0 4px; letter-spacing: -0.5px; }

  .subtitle { font-size: 15px; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 28px; }

  h2 {
    font-size: 19px;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 38px 0 12px;
    padding-bottom: 8px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  h3 { font-size: 16px; margin: 22px 0 6px; }

  /* Before / after score cards */
  .scores { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; margin: 24px 0; }

  .score-box {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 22px;
    text-align: center;
    background: #FAFCFB;
  }

  .score-box h3 { margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: 13px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--muted); }

  .gauge {
    width: 104px;
    height: 104px;
    margin: 0 auto 10px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 8px solid #0CCE6B;
    background: #E8F8EF;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font: 700 34px ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    color: #08803F;
  }

  .score-note { font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); margin: 0; }
  .score-note b { color: var(--text); }
  .score-note b.fail { color: var(--bad); }
  .score-note b.pass { color: #08803F; }

  .callout {
    background: var(--accent-tint);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0;
    padding: 14px 18px;
    margin: 18px 0;
  }

  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 12px 0 18px; font-size: 15px; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 8px 10px; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  th { background: var(--accent-tint); }
  td.c { text-align: center; white-space: nowrap; }
  .fail { color: var(--bad); font-weight: 700; }
  .pass { color: #08803F; font-weight: 700; }

  code {
    background: #F1F5F4;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    font-size: 13.5px;
    font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
  }

  pre {
    background: #F6F8F7;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 12px 14px;
    font: 13px/1.5 ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: 4px 0 12px;
  }

  .tag { display: inline-block; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; padding: 1px 10px; border-radius: 999px; margin-bottom: 2px; }
  .tag.before { background: var(--bad-tint); color: var(--bad); }
  .tag.after { background: #E3F6EA; color: #08803F; }

  .screenshot-box {
    margin: 18px 0;
    text-align: center;
    background: #FAFCFB;
    padding: 18px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .screenshot-box p { font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 10px; }
  .screenshot-box img { max-width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid #CBD5D1; }

  a { color: var(--accent); }
  a:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px; border-radius: 4px; }

  .footer {
    margin-top: 44px;
    padding-top: 20px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-align: center;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .container { padding: 26px 20px; }
    .scores { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    h1 { font-size: 25px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<main class="container">
  <h1>Accessibility Audit Report</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">LifeOS (Team 9 project) · Aranjmaa Lkhamaa, 202637428 · Web Programming, Gachon University</p>

  <div class="scores">
    <div class="score-box">
      <h3>Before</h3>
      <div class="gauge" aria-hidden="true">100</div>
      <p class="score-note">Lighthouse score <b>100 / 100</b><br>Manual checks failed: <b class="fail">5 of 10</b></p>
    </div>
    <div class="score-box">
      <h3>After</h3>
      <div class="gauge" aria-hidden="true">100</div>
      <p class="score-note">Lighthouse score <b>100 / 100</b><br>Manual checks failed: <b class="pass">0 of 10</b></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>1. Audit overview</h2>
  <p>I ran a Lighthouse Accessibility audit on our team project page, <a href="../lifeos.html">LifeOS</a>. I checked every part of the app: Overview, My Life, Plan, the record window and the Add form. All of them scored <strong>100/100</strong>, which is above the 85 target.</p>
  <div class="callout">Lighthouse says that automatic detection finds only part of the problems, and it lists <strong>10 items to check manually</strong>. I tested those 10 items with the keyboard, and <strong>5 of them failed</strong>. The most serious problem: keyboard users could not open any record, because the record rows were clickable <code>&lt;div&gt;</code> elements. Lighthouse cannot detect this.</div>

  <h2>2. Issues found</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Lighthouse manual check</th><th>Problem I found</th><th class="c">Before</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Interactive controls are keyboard focusable</td><td>Record rows in My Life, Plan and “Linked records” were <code>&lt;div&gt;</code>s, so Tab skipped them.</td><td class="c fail">Fail</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Focus is directed to new content</td><td>When a record or the Add form opened, focus stayed on the page behind it.</td><td class="c fail">Fail</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Offscreen content is hidden from assistive technology</td><td>While the window was open, Tab went to the dimmed page behind it, and the window had no dialog role.</td><td class="c fail">Fail</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Custom controls have associated labels</td><td>The search box had only a placeholder and no <code>&lt;label&gt;</code>.</td><td class="c fail">Fail</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Interactive elements indicate their purpose and state</td><td>The selected page and filter were shown only by colour, and messages were not read aloud.</td><td class="c fail">Fail</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>3. What I changed</h2>

  <h3>Fix 1 — Div rows became real buttons</h3>
  <span class="tag before">Before</span>
  <pre>&lt;div class="item click" data-a="open"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Wireless headphones&lt;/b&gt;...&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</pre>
  <span class="tag after">After</span>
  <pre>&lt;button type="button" class="item click" data-a="open"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;b&gt;Wireless headphones&lt;/b&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;</pre>

  <h3>Fix 2 — The record and Add windows became accessible dialogs</h3>
  <p>Focus now moves into the window when it opens. Tab stays inside it, Escape closes it, and focus returns to the button that opened it.</p>
  <span class="tag before">Before</span>
  <pre>&lt;div class="md" id="md"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</pre>
  <span class="tag after">After</span>
  <pre>&lt;div class="md" id="md" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="md-title" tabindex="-1"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
// show(): remember the opener, move focus into the dialog
// close(): return focus to the opener; Tab / Shift+Tab stay inside the dialog</pre>

  <h3>Fix 3 — Label for the search box</h3>
  <span class="tag before">Before</span>
  <pre>&lt;input class="in" id="q" placeholder="Search your records"&gt;</pre>
  <span class="tag after">After</span>
  <pre>&lt;label class="sr-only" for="q"&gt;Search your records&lt;/label&gt;
&lt;input class="in" id="q" type="search" placeholder="Search your records"&gt;</pre>

  <h3>Fix 4 — Selected page and filter announced</h3>
  <span class="tag before">Before</span>
  <pre>&lt;button class="nv on"&gt;My Life&lt;/button&gt;      &lt;button class="chip on"&gt;All&lt;/button&gt;</pre>
  <span class="tag after">After</span>
  <pre>&lt;button class="nv on" aria-current="page"&gt;My Life&lt;/button&gt;      &lt;button class="chip on" aria-pressed="true"&gt;All&lt;/button&gt;</pre>

  <h3>Fix 5 — Messages read aloud</h3>
  <span class="tag before">Before</span>
  <pre>&lt;div class="toast" id="toast"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</pre>
  <span class="tag after">After</span>
  <pre>&lt;div class="toast" id="toast" role="status" aria-live="polite"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</pre>

  <h3>Fix 6 — Visible focus ring and skip link</h3>
  <pre>&lt;a class="skip" href="#main"&gt;Skip to main content&lt;/a&gt;
:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--sage-d); outline-offset: 2px; }</pre>

  <h2>4. Results</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Check</th><th class="c">Before</th><th class="c">After</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Lighthouse Accessibility score</td><td class="c">100</td><td class="c pass">100</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Lighthouse automated audits that apply and pass</td><td class="c">10</td><td class="c pass">19</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Lighthouse manual checks that pass</td><td class="c fail">5 / 10</td><td class="c pass">10 / 10</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Records that can be opened with the keyboard</td><td class="c fail">0</td><td class="c pass">All</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Keyboard trap (bonus): can always leave a window</td><td class="c pass">Yes</td><td class="c pass">Yes</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Tab stays inside an open window</td><td class="c fail">No</td><td class="c pass">Yes</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Focus returns to the opener after closing</td><td class="c fail">No</td><td class="c pass">Yes</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>5. Lighthouse audit screenshots</h2>
  <div class="screenshot-box">
    <p>Before: score 100/100 and the 10 items to check manually</p>
    <a href="audit-before.png" target="_blank"><img src="audit-before.png" alt="Lighthouse report before the fixes: Accessibility score 100, with 10 additional items to check manually"></a>
  </div>
  <div class="screenshot-box">
    <p>After: score 100/100 and 19 passed audits</p>
    <a href="audit-after.png" target="_blank"><img src="audit-after.png" alt="Lighthouse report after the fixes: Accessibility score 100, with 19 passed audits"></a>
  </div>

  <h2>6. Conclusion</h2>
  <p>LifeOS scored 100/100 from the start, but testing it with the keyboard showed real problems that Lighthouse cannot detect.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Changing <code>&lt;div&gt;</code> rows to real buttons now lets keyboard users open every record.</li>
    <li>Turning the windows into proper dialogs keeps focus where the user expects it.</li>
    <li>The search box now has a label.</li>
    <li>The selected page and filter, and status messages, are now announced.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The score stays at 100, all 10 manual checks now pass, and the design did not change.</p>

  <p class="footer">Aranjmaa Lkhamaa · 202637428 · Team 9 · Web Programming, Gachon University</p>
</main>

</body>
